## What this adds
8 MCP tools over the Weave Agents observability API (OTel/GenAI agent spans), a data plane SEPARATE from classic Weave calls. Single new module: mcp_tools/agents.py (tools + descriptions + helpers). Registered in server.py and added to _WEAVE_TOOL_NAMES so WANDB_MCP_ENABLE_WEAVE_TOOLS=false disables them too.

## Refactor (post-first-draft, in response to "re-use existing code / agents.py confusing")
The first draft had a separate weave_api/agents_client.py (AgentsApiClient class) + a _run(tool_name, params, lambda c: c.method(...)) envelope in agents.py -- non-idiomatic (triple param repetition; a client class for plain JSON POSTs that no other simple tool in this repo uses). Refactored to match mcp_tools/count_traces.py exactly: deleted agents_client.py entirely; each tool now builds a request-body dict inline and calls one shared helper _agents_request(tool_name, path, body, track_params) that does the basic-auth POST via get_retry_session(), wrapped in track_tool_execution, with structured_error mapping + _truncate_response. Net: -332 lines (client gone) and agents.py slimmed ~116 lines. This is THE answer to "is this how the rest of the repo has it instrumented?" -- yes, count_traces.py is the precedent (direct basic-auth POST to /calls/query_stats, no client class).

## API contract (reverse-engineered; NOT in local weave 0.52.35)
Source of truth: weave/trace_server/agents/types.py @ github.com/wandb/weave (master). Endpoints confirmed via sdks/node/src/generated/traceServerApi.ts + Node SDK request cassettes (sdks/node/src/__tests__/__cassettes__/weaveclient_*.yaml -- real request/response JSON against https://trace.wandb.ai).
Read endpoints (all POST, plain JSON, NOT JSONL-streamed like /calls/stream_query):
  /agents/query                      -> {project_id,filters{agent_name},sort_by[{field,direction}],limit,offset,include_costs} -> {agents,total_count}
  /agents/agent-versions/query       -> {versions,total_count}
  /agents/spans/query                -> {project_id,query(Mongo \$expr),sort_by,limit,offset,started_after,started_before,include_details,include_costs} -> {spans,total_count}
  /agents/spans/stats                -> {project_id,start,end,granularity,timezone,group_by,metrics[AgentSpanStatsMetricSpec]} -> {columns,rows,...}
  /agents/spans/custom-attrs/schema  -> {attributes,has_more}
  /agents/search                     -> {project_id,query,trace_id,conversation_id,agent_name,roles,...} -> {results,total_conversations}
  /agents/traces/chat                -> {project_id,trace_id,include_feedback} -> AgentTraceChatRes{messages[typed timeline],...}
  /agents/conversations/chat         -> {project_id,conversation_id,limit,offset,include_feedback} -> {turns:[AgentTraceChatRes],...}
Ingest (write, not exposed): /agents/otel/v1/traces. Auth: HTTP Basic, base64(\":\"+api_key). project_id = \"entity/project\".

## Key design decisions
- Do NOT import weave agent types: pinned weave 0.52.35 predates them; MCP already speaks raw HTTP to the trace server. Request bodies are dicts (None values dropped via _drop_none so server defaults apply); responses returned as dicts.
- _best_effort_viewer(): the analytics viewer fetch (WandBApiManager.get_api().viewer) is a SEPARATE GraphQL call that can raise WandbApiFailedError 'relogin required' independently of the data request. count_traces.py calls it unguarded; here it is wrapped try/except -> None so analytics identity NEVER breaks a data tool. This is a deliberate, justified divergence from count_traces -- see Errors below (it crashed live verify when left unguarded).
- _truncate_response trims the largest list field (_TRUNCATABLE_LIST_KEYS, most-verbose first) to MAX_RESPONSE_TOKENS (reuses TraceProcessor.estimate_tokens) and adds a _truncation note. Does NOT reuse enforce_token_budget (that one is calls/trace-shaped).
- Stats tool: _normalize_stats_metrics turns user-friendly metric inputs into AgentSpanStatsMetricSpec dicts. String 'input_tokens' -> {source:field}; derived names (duration_ms,total_tokens,is_error,is_invocation,total_cost_usd,input_cost_usd,output_cost_usd) -> {source:derived}; boolean derived -> aggregations ['count_true'] (sum/avg invalid for boolean per server _ALLOWED_AGGS_BY_TYPE). Full spec dicts pass through.
- query_agent_spans: agent_name shortcut becomes a Mongo \$eq on agent_name, AND-combined with any caller query. include_details defaults False (raw OTel dumps are huge).

## Errors / dead ends
- Initially pursued the THREADS API (/threads/stream_query) -- WRONG; user wanted the Agents API. Different (older) feature.
- REFACTOR REGRESSION: when matching count_traces exactly I replaced _best_effort_viewer() with unguarded WandBApiManager.get_api().viewer. Live verify then crashed with wandb...WandbApiFailedError: relogin required -- the viewer/analytics fetch took down the whole tool. Fix: restored the guarded _best_effort_viewer(). Lesson: count_traces is the structural precedent but its unguarded viewer call is a latent bug we should not copy.
- Local env had no venv / no python3.11 / no uv / no gh / no gt. Installed uv via astral script; uv venv --python 3.11 && uv sync && uv sync --extra test. gh/gt absent -> first PR created via GitHub REST API using git credential helper token.
- `ls` is aliased to eza in the interactive shell -> use find/Glob, not ls.

